#: content/en/posts/2024/2024-roadmap.md:0
msgid "What We're Up To In 2024"
msgstr ""

#: content/en/posts/2024/2024-roadmap.md:5
msgid ""
"It's 2024 already, and even already March. Like last year, we had a video "
"call with all sponsored developers, artists and volunteers to discuss what "
"we achieved last year, figure out the biggest issues we're facing and set "
"the priorities for this year."
msgstr ""

#: content/en/posts/2024/2024-roadmap.md:8
msgid "Challenges"
msgstr ""

#: content/en/posts/2024/2024-roadmap.md:11
msgid ""
"A very serious issue is that the maintainer of the Android and ChromeOS port "
"of Krita has become too busy to work on Krita full-time. The Android and "
"ChromeOS versions of Krita both use the Android platform, and that platform "
"changes often and arbitrarily. This means that Sharaf has spent almost all "
"of his time keeping Krita running on Android (and ChromeOS), instead of, as "
"we had planned, work on a dedicated tablet user interface for Krita on "
"Android. And since that maintenance work now is not being done, we're having "
"a really big problem there. Additionally, since KDE has retired the binary "
"factory and moved binary builds to invent.kde.org's continuous integration "
"system, we don't have automatic builds for Android anymore."
msgstr ""

#: content/en/posts/2024/2024-roadmap.md:13
msgid ""
"We've also lost another sponsored developer. They were sick for quite some "
"time, but recently they blogged they had started to work a different job. "
"Since they were especially working on maintaining the libraries Krita is "
"dependent on and were very good at upstreaming fixes, they will also really "
"be missed."
msgstr ""

#: content/en/posts/2024/2024-roadmap.md:15
msgid ""
"Finally, we got Krita into the Apple MacOS store last year. However, two "
"years ago, Krita's maintainer, that's me, changed her legal name. Now the "
"certificates needed to sign the package for the store have expired, and we "
"needed to create new certificates. Those have to have the signer's current "
"legal name, and for some reason, it's proving really hard get the store to "
"allow that the same developer, with the same ID and code but a different "
"legal name to upload packages. We're working on that."
msgstr ""

#: content/en/posts/2024/2024-roadmap.md:17
msgid "What We Did Last Year"
msgstr ""

#: content/en/posts/2024/2024-roadmap.md:19
msgid ""
"Of course, we released Krita 5.2 and two bugfix releases for Krita 5.2. "
"We'll do at least one other bugfix release before we release Krita 5.3."
msgstr ""

#: content/en/posts/2024/2024-roadmap.md:21
msgid ""
"The audio system for Krita's animation feature got completely overhauled, "
"ported away from Qt's QtMultimedia system to MLT, The storyboard feature got "
"improved a lot, we gained JPEG-XL support just in time for Google's Chrome "
"team to decide to drop it, because there was nobody supporting it... We also "
"refactored the system we use to build all dependent libraries on all "
"platforms. Well, work on MacOS is still going on, with PyQt being a problem "
"point. Of course, there were a lot of other things going on as well."
msgstr ""

#: content/en/posts/2024/2024-roadmap.md:23
msgid ""
"Wolthera started rewriting the text object, and mostly finished that and now "
"is working on the tool to actually write, modify and typeset text. This is a "
"huge change with very impressive results!"
msgstr ""

#: content/en/posts/2024/2024-roadmap.md:25
msgid "What We Hope To Do This Year"
msgstr ""

#: content/en/posts/2024/2024-roadmap.md:27
msgid "Parts of this list is from last year, part of it is new."
msgstr ""

#: content/en/posts/2024/2024-roadmap.md:29
msgid ""
"One big caveat: now that the KDE project has released the first version of "
"KDE Frameworks for Qt6, porting Krita to Qt6 is going to have to happen. "
"This is a big project, not just because of disappearing functions, but very "
"much because of the changes to the support for GPU rendering. On Windows, "
"OpenGL drivers are pretty buggy, and because of that, Qt5 offered the "
"possibility to use the Angle compatibility layer between applications that "
"use OpenGL and the native Direct3D library for GPU rendering. That's gone, "
"and unless we rewrite our GPU rendering system, we need to put Angle back "
"into the stack."
msgstr ""

#: content/en/posts/2024/2024-roadmap.md:31
msgid ""
"All in all, it's pretty likely that porting to Qt6 will take a lot of time "
"away from us implementing fun new features. But when that is done we can "
"start working on a tablet-friendly user interface, provided we can still "
"release Krita for Android."
msgstr ""

#: content/en/posts/2024/2024-roadmap.md:33
msgid "That's not to say we don't want to implement fun new featurs!"
msgstr ""

#: content/en/posts/2024/2024-roadmap.md:35
msgid "Here's the shortlist:"
msgstr ""

#: content/en/posts/2024/2024-roadmap.md:37
msgid ""
"Implement a system to create flexible text balloons and integrate that with "
"the text object so the text flows into the balloons"
msgstr ""

#: content/en/posts/2024/2024-roadmap.md:38
msgid "Implement a new layer type, for comic book Frameworks"
msgstr ""

#: content/en/posts/2024/2024-roadmap.md:39
msgid ""
"Provide integration with Blender. (This is less urgent, though, since there "
"is a very useful third-party plugin for that already: [Blender Layer]"
"(https://github.com/Yuntokon/BlenderLayer/))"
msgstr ""

#: content/en/posts/2024/2024-roadmap.md:40
msgid ""
"Replace the current docker system with something more flexible, and "
"maintained."
msgstr ""

#: content/en/posts/2024/2024-roadmap.md:41
msgid "Implement a system to provide tool presets"
msgstr ""

#: content/en/posts/2024/2024-roadmap.md:42
msgid "Create a new user interface for handling palettes"
msgstr ""

#: content/en/posts/2024/2024-roadmap.md:43
msgid "Add an animation audio waveform display"
msgstr ""

#: content/en/posts/2024/2024-roadmap.md:44
msgid "Add support for animation reference frame workflow."
msgstr ""

#: content/en/posts/2024/2024-roadmap.md:46
msgid ""
"We also discussed using the GPU for improving performance. One original idea "
"was to use the GPU for brushes, but the artists argued that the brush "
"performance is fine, and what's way too slow are the liquefy transform tool, "
"transform masks and some filters. In the end, Dmitry decided to investigate"
msgstr ""

#: content/en/posts/2024/2024-roadmap.md:48
msgid "optimizing transform masks on the GPU"
msgstr ""

#: content/en/posts/2024/2024-roadmap.md:50
msgid ""
"And there's the most controversial thing of all: should we add AI features "
"to Krita? We have had several heated discussions amongst developers and "
"artists on the mailing list and on invent.kde.org."
msgstr ""

#: content/en/posts/2024/2024-roadmap.md:52
msgid ""
"The artists in the meeting argued that generative AI is worthless and would "
"at best lead to bland, repetitive templates, but that assistive AI could be "
"useful. In order to figure out whether that's true, we started investigating "
"one particular project: AI-assisted inking of sketches. This is useful, "
"could replace a tedious step when doing art while still retaining the "
"artistic individuality. Whether it will actually make it to Krita is "
"uncertain of course, but the investigation will hopefully help us understand "
"better the issue, the possibilities and the problems."
msgstr ""

#: content/en/posts/2024/2024-roadmap.md:54
msgid ""
"Note: we won't be implementing anything that uses models trained on scraped "
"images and we will make sure that the carbon footprint of the feature "
"doesn't exceed its usefulness."
msgstr ""

#: content/en/posts/2024/monthly-update-13.md:0
